## What the numbers set

- `ROW_STRUCT_BYTES = 5_760` — line (b): 5,642 B of live heap per rendered row
  against 88 B of row text. Rounded *up* rather than to the nearest KiB, because
  a charge under the truth makes the cap larger than the number printed on it.
- `DEFAULT_RETAINED_BYTES = 32 MiB` — the ceiling on one view's rendered
  content. At the measured shape that is ~5.8k retained rows: ~144 screens of
  scrollback at 40 rows a screen, ~0.5 MiB of visible text, about a fifth of a
  long pass — against the 166 MiB the store held with no cap at all.
- The journal costs ~3.5 MiB of *disk* per pass at this shape and no memory to
  speak of, which is what makes it an acceptable home for everything the cap
  throws away.
